        "Choking with an effective cough is encouraged and nothing else; an ineffective cough gets five back blows alternating with five abdominal thrusts in adults and children over one year, and five back blows alternating with five chest thrusts — never abdominal — in infants; the collapsed casualty gets resuscitation starting with compressions and no blind finger sweeps.",
        "Anaphylaxis — rapid airway, breathing or circulation problems with or without skin changes — is treated by calling for help, removing the trigger, lying the patient flat with the legs raised, and intramuscular adrenaline 1 in 1,000 into the anterolateral thigh: 0.5 mg over twelve years, 0.3 mg at six to twelve, 0.15 mg at six months to six years, repeated after five minutes, with oxygen, a fluid bolus and monitoring; antihistamines and steroids are not first line; observe six to twenty-four hours, record the allergy, and arrange auto-injectors and referral.",
