          alt: "Palliative care and hospice are not the same thing. Palliative care runs from diagnosis to death and bereavement, alongside curative treatment, from diagnosis onward; any age, any stage, any life-limiting illness — cancer, HIV, heart failure, sickle cell. Hospice covers the last months: a subset, comfort-focused care when cure is no longer the goal. All hospice care is palliative; not all palliative care is hospice. Total pain has four dimensions — treat all four: physical, psychological, social, spiritual. Morphine alone will not settle pain that is really fear, debt or unfinished business.",
